# Variant proof battle 6 of 6 — the Colossus (docs/ENEMY_ROSTER.md).

id: nv-06-dead-weight
number: 706
name: Dead Weight
description: A Colossus that Push 1 and Push 2 both fail to move. Pull is unaffected — bring the Threadcaster or bring a lot of attacks.
design: The question: what do you do when the board is not a weapon?
design: Push resistance 2. Push 1 does nothing and Push 2 does nothing, so the Vanguard's basic shove and Bull Rush are both dead against it as openers — the two verbs this game normally answers everything with. Only a Stagger unlocks it: staggered, Bull Rush is an effective Push 3 and moves it exactly 1. Pull is untouched, because resistance is a Push rule and not a weight rule. The Threadcaster is therefore the answer, and the pit sitting on row 0 two tiles east of the Colossus is the payoff — Reel resolves every tile on the way, so a pull along that row puts 10 HP over the lip.
design: The Mobile Anchor is the second lesson in the same sentence: the shrug you can ignore at Move 1 arrives at Move 2 while the fight is still on.
retired: bestiary fixtures, not designs — the enemies they prove are redeployed into the curated set

spawn c = Colossus
spawn n = MobileAnchor

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  ..c.O.B
  ......B
  .^....B
  .......
  .....^.
  A....H.
  AA.n...
